  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-25" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6. Refer to Note 7, &#8220;Debt and Credit Agreements&#8221; of the accompanying &#8220;Notes to Financial Statements&#8221; for discussion of BGE&#8217;s borrowings and other credit agreements in 2026, including the May 22, 2026 issuance of $925 million of long-term notes. The authorization for the issuances of long-term debt or equity securities are Maryland Public Service Commission (MDPSC) Order No. 91535, authorizing up to $2.2 billion in long-term financing. The MDPSC Order No. 91535 financing authority became effective on February 20, 2025 and does not have an expiration date. As of June 30, 2026, BGE had $925 million under Order No. 91535. BGE also has authorization under the authority granted by the FERC in Docket ES25-20250908-5162 to issue up to $900 million of short-term debt, which expires on December 31, 2027.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-26" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;7. None&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-27" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;8. In March 2026, BGE had a 3% general wage increase. This change is estimated to result in a total annual overall increase in operations and maintenance expense of approximately $6.8 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-28" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9. Refer to Pages 122-123, Notes to Financial Statements: Note 2 &#8211; Regulatory Matters and Note 9 &#8211; Commitments and Contingencies, &#8220;Litigation and Regulatory Matters&#8221; section.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
